{"success": true, "name": "arc-task-delta-inference", "file": "references/task-29b1b5eb-edge-extension.md", "content": "# Edge-extension evidence from a heterogeneous ARC stream

In a stream instance with varied palettes and grid sizes, demonstrations consistently modified only cells immediately to the right of an existing horizontal same-color run, recoloring the formerly background suffix to color 1. Examples included short left-edge runs extended to the right boundary and right-edge-adjacent bars in different locations; complete bars remained unchanged. A test with sparse/colorful motifs still followed this family: only the end of the horizontal run at the right edge was converted, leaving the rest intact.

Process lesson: do not spend the full demo budget automatically. Extract each pair's exact changed coordinates, compare with all unchanged candidate runs, and formulate a measurable selector (e.g., a bar ending short of the right boundary versus full-width bars) before another request. Even when a rule is evident, validate the predicted row and exact suffix length against every demo. Keep the session-specific rule as evidence, not as a universal task-ID mapping.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen/play/users/u020/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-task-delta-inference/references/task-29b1b5eb-edge-extension.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-ledger", "file": "references/score-aware-feedback-loop.md", "content": "# Score-aware ARC feedback loop

In a puzzle stream, both a wrong submission and each demo request have explicit costs, and unresolved instances may incur the full budget. Do not treat a request as a default holding action after an incorrect answer. First integrate the received pair: identify all changed cells, establish what remains unchanged, and assess whether the current candidate rule exactly replays every demo. In this instance, two speculative extensions were rejected; the next returned example showed a long diagonal extension from a small motif, but did not establish that this rule explained the earlier demonstrations or the test. Similar-looking patterns and recurring task IDs are retrieval cues, not answer evidence.

A further request is worthwhile only when a precise question can be stated and its possible answers could change the test prediction. A submission is warranted only when the candidate has exact multi-demo support. When neither condition holds, avoid cycling between unsupported guesses and vague requests: reassess task class and representation, then choose deliberately under the scoring tradeoff. Keep the required one-action JSON format on every puzzle turn.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen/play/users/u020/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-ledger/references/score-aware-feedback-loop.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-incorrect-submission-recovery", "file": "references/continual-turn-lessons.md", "content": "# Continual ARC turn completeness and evidence boundaries

In continual puzzle interfaces, each message—including incorrect feedback—requires one legal action JSON on the final line. A thoughtful diagnosis without a valid action leaves the turn incomplete.

After a rejection, use references from previously encountered sessions only as process cautions. They are not evidence that this task shares the referenced transformation; do not transplant specific rules or guessed output grids. Reconstruct the current examples' deltas and representations, and demand exact replay of every available demo before another submission. If no supported candidate exists, request a demo only when it answers a concrete ambiguity that could change the output.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen/play/users/u020/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-incorrect-submission-recovery/references/continual-turn-lessons.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-evidence-recovery", "file": "references/task-29b1b5eb-instance-review.md", "content": "# Task 29b1b5eb: fresh-instance evidence caution

